Practical 11 :-
Represent a Map-Coloring problem as a CSP and solve it using backtracking search

Prolog Code:-
color(red).
color(green).
color(blue).

different(X,Y) :- X \= Y.

map(A,B,C,D) :-
    color(A),
    color(B),
    color(C),
    color(D),

    different(A,B),
    different(A,C),
    different(B,C),
    different(B,D),
    different(C,D).

Output Query:-
1.) ?- map(A, B, C, D).
2.) ?- map(red, red, blue, green).

Output:-
1.) A = red,
    B = green,
    C = blue,
    D = red.
2.) false.
